::heading level=1 id=virtual-check
Pointer Resolution Check
::end

::paragraph id=virtual-check-summary
A `.dx` file on disk is one line — `~ dx1 <sha256>` — and the content lives in the workspace store. The rule everything rests on is that the resolver always hands back the true document, whoever is asking. A caller that sees a pointer where a document belongs, or nothing where content exists, is a regression.
::end

::html id=virtual-check-table
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Who is reading</th><th>Through</th><th>What must come back</th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td>A person in the editor</td><td><code>doc-wasm</code></td><td>The rendered page.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>dx text</code> / <code>dx render</code></td><td><code>doc-cli::workspace</code></td><td>The document.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>An agent calling <code>dx_read</code></td><td><code>doc-cli::mcp</code></td><td>The page, as images.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>git diff</code> on a <code>.dx</code></td><td><code>dx textconv</code></td><td>The document, not the digest.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>A reader on github.com</td><td><code>editor/github/resolve.js</code></td><td>The document, from the page's own origin.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
::end

::heading level=2 id=virtual-check-store-heading
What lives where
::end

